Winds (F1 and F4) to be discarded later. \n\nSo the answer would be to Play B5.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Discarding B5 helps streamline the hand towards a potential Full Flush or multiple Chows in the W suit, while removing a non-meld tile that doesn't contribute to high-scoring patterns.  \nReason: B5 is a single tile not part of any sequence or meld, and discarding it reduces non-suit tiles, aiding in forming a cohesive W-suit hand. The W tiles (4-9) can form multiple Chows (e.g., W4-W5-W6, W7-W8-W9), and retaining F4 (2 copies) allows for potential Wind Pung or pair formation later.  \nAnswer: Play B5"}
